// Believer — Imagine Dragons
// Sample .clyr file demonstrating the format's supported features.
//
// Word-level timing inside each chorus line is an ESTIMATE (evenly/tastefully
// spread across that line's real start/end window from the source timestamps)
// since only phrase-level timing was available, not authoritative per-word data.
//
// "Flying"/"falling"/"stairs" are approximated with rapid, statically-positioned
// word cues (no real motion/animation exists in this version of the format —
// that's an explicitly deferred future feature, see CLYR_FORMAT.md).

@font: "Inter"
@size: 32px
@color: "#FFFFFF"
@align: center

// ── Verse 1 ──────────────────────────────────────────────
[00:07.774] -> [00:09.188] First things first
[00:09.188] -> [00:12.194] I'ma say all the words inside my head
[00:12.194] -> [00:14.453] I'm fired up and tired of
[00:14.453] -> [00:18.074] The way that things have been, oh-ooh
[00:18.074] -> [00:22.885] The way that things have been, oh-ooh

// ── Verse 2 ──────────────────────────────────────────────
[00:22.885] -> [00:24.701] Second thing second
[00:24.701] -> [00:27.273] Don't you tell me what you think that I could be
[00:27.273] -> [00:29.483] I'm the one at the sail
[00:29.483] -> [00:33.466] I'm the master of my sea, oh-ooh
[00:33.466] -> [00:38.149] The master of my sea, oh-ooh

// ── Pre-Chorus 1 ─────────────────────────────────────────
[00:38.149] -> [00:40.073] I was broken from a young age
[00:40.073] -> [00:41.967] Taking my sulkin' to the masses
[00:41.967] -> [00:43.733] Writing my poems for the few
[00:43.733] -> [00:45.780] That look at me, took to me, shook at me, feelin' me
[00:45.780] -> [00:47.674] Singing from heartache from the pain
[00:47.674] -> [00:49.516] Taking my message from the veins
[00:49.516] -> [00:51.438] Speaking my lesson from the brain
[00:51.438] -> [00:54.695] Seeing the beauty through the...

